      "quote": "It is not always appropriate to insist on provision of turnover and/or marketing figures. Examiners must always consider the commercial realities relevant to the claimed goods and/or services when assessing evidence and maintaining grounds for rejection. Sometimes, the capacity to distinguish of a trade mark might be more accurately demonstrated by metrics other than revenue or promotional expenditure figures."
    },
    {
      "ref": "TMM/Part23/4/4/1/1",
      "quote": "Other metrics that are relevant may include website and social media analytic figures, funds managed, raised, or distributed by an entity (e.g. in the case of a investment company or a charity), or viewership figures for videos, podcasts etc."
