    {
      "ref": "TMM/Part23/4/4/1~1",
      "quote": "Massive turnover may compensate for short use, likewise, long use may compensate for small turnover, especially in relation to trade marks with some inherent adaptation to distinguish. However, total turnover must be considered in the context of the relevant market and balanced against unit cost before a decision can be made on this issue. Applicants should be encouraged to supply information on unit costs and perhaps market share to help support their case."
    },
